1. afplay vs. PyAudio: Since PyAudio was generating issyes because of the PortAudio library dependency used on MacOS intel chip, i switched to afplay wich uses macOS built in native audio port.
2. From "while data"  #Starts -> Works -> Dies. tts_model.tts_to_file(...) subprocess.run(["afplay", "output.wav"]) to "while true" (loop/Dynamic Script) 
    entrada = input(">> ")  #Process AI (Decide which character the user is adressing, adjusting the ollama local model, choosing the voice in funtion of the previously selected) -> Generate Audio -> Play Audio
    subprocess.run(["afplay", "output.wav"]) (if it is a subprocess, it means the script it obligated to wait until the process is complete in order to contiue running) 
